# Code owners (W1 R7 P8 review round 2, P8-R2-01; final check, P8-F-04).
# With "Require review from Code Owners" on in the default branch ruleset, a
# change to these paths needs the maintainer's review. They decide what the
# release workflow runs with a secret, a write permission, or the npm OIDC
# token, and what a green release or CI check means: the workflows and this
# file, every build, release, and gate script with its policy inputs and
# vendored schemas, the tests and gate corpora the checks run (golden
# harness, conversion eval, planted-failure fixtures), the package manifest,
# lockfile, and npm and TypeScript settings, the SBOM policy documents, and
# the product files the build scripts read to decide the package content.
# test/codeowners.test.ts computes that set from the workflows and the
# scripts and fails when a file is outside every pattern here.
# See toolkits/buildos/SECURITY.md, Owner Settings for Releases.
